             Moving to Somerville? 
 Moving is always a stressful time, and finding what you need to know in a new city can be overwhelming. to help, Somerville has created a New Resident's Guide. This guide is a one-stop shop for everything a first-time resident of Somerville needs to know - and is even useful for long-time residents looking for basic information about utilities, trash and recycling, parking, and more.  
 New Resident's Guide 
 Trash and Recycling Schedule 
 Always know when your trash and recycling will be picked up with our online calendar. 
 Find Your Trash & Street Sweeping Schedule 
 Parking Questions? 
 Somerville is a busy place and parking can be complicated for new and long-term residents alike. Check on parking rules and regulations as well as find a map of road closures and constructions at ParkSomerville:  
 Visit ParkSomerville 
 Sign Up for Alerts 
 City Alerts share timely information about emergencies, construction and road closures in your area, and other important community news. You can choose to receive alerts either by email, phone, text, or all three in multiple languages. 
 Set Up City Alerts 
 311 Has the Answers 
 Somerville's 311 Service Center is the place to go to make a service request, ask Somerville-specific questions, and more. Learn about 311 and download the app below. 
