 Mail-in Ballot Counting 
 We will count any vote-by-mail ballots received after 5 pm on Election Day, Thursday the 12th, during a post-election count in the Council Chambers, from 9 am until it is complete. The Elections Department will also accept and count all vote-by-mail ballots time-stamped on Election Day, November 3rd, but received before Friday, November 6th, during the post-election count; this exception applies only to general state/federal elections.  

   







             Hours 
